%% C4 level 4 (code): UML sequence diagram of approving a venue booking request
%% (SCRUM-40, SCRUM-41, SCRUM-84). backend/app/venues/routes.py: approve_booking.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor VS as Venue Staff
    participant FE as Front-End App
    participant API as Venue and Booking API
    participant PERM as Roles and Permissions
    participant SCH as Venue Scheduling
    participant DB as Database
    participant MQ as Message Broker

    VS->>FE: Approve booking request
    FE->>API: POST /api/venues/bookings/{id}/approve (JWT)
    API->>PERM: Holds the Venue Staff role? (role read from DB)
    PERM-->>API: Yes
    API->>DB: Lock booking and venue rows
    API->>SCH: Occupied period = [start - setup, end + turnaround)
    API->>DB: Confirmed bookings, unexpired holds and blocks overlapping it
    alt Conflict found
        API-->>FE: 409, with the conflicting period
    else No conflict
        API->>DB: Booking = confirmed + in-app notification (one commit)
        Note over DB: Exclusion constraint also refuses<br/>overlapping confirmed bookings
        API->>MQ: Queue email to coordinator (after commit)
        API-->>FE: 200 Approved
    end
